To: amd-gfx-PD4FTy7X32lNgt0PjOBp9y5qC8QIuHrW@public.gmane.org
Subject: [PATCH] drm/amdgpu: fix VM size reporting on Raven

Raven doesn't have an VCE block and so also no buggy VCE firmware.

Signed-off-by: Christian K=F6nig <christian.koenig-5C7GfCeVMHo@public.gmane.org>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/amdgpu_kms.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/amdgpu_kms.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/=
amdgpu/amdgpu_kms.c
index 7d3d76a1a9dd..2ecb883bdd41 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/amdgpu_kms.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/amdgpu_kms.c
@@ -619,7 +619,8 @@ static int amdgpu_info_ioctl(struct drm_device *dev, vo=
id *data, struct drm_file
                 vm_size -=3D AMDGPU_VA_RESERVED_SIZE;

                 /* Older VCE FW versions are buggy and can handle only 40b=
its */
-               if (adev->vce.fw_version < AMDGPU_VCE_FW_53_45)
+               if (adev->vce.fw_version &&
+                   adev->vce.fw_version < AMDGPU_VCE_FW_53_45)
                         vm_size =3D min(vm_size, 1ULL << 40);

                 dev_info.virtual_address_offset =3D AMDGPU_VA_RESERVED_SIZ=
E;
--
2.17.1

